course: dictionary
lesson: 16060
title: A word for a singer in a band
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vocalist is a singer, especially one who sings with a band or group. Vocal means to do with the voice, so a vocalist makes music with their voice. «The lead vocalist sang the first verse alone.» Lead tells you this singer is the main one out front.
explain: Look at the words around vocalist to check its meaning. Lead, backing and guest are small clues that tell you what kind of singer is meant. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The singer sang the first verse alone» still makes sense, so vocalist means singer.
explain: Vocalist is a noun, a word for a person or thing, and its plural is vocalists. «The backing vocalists sang softly behind her.» Backing means they support the main singer, so they sing behind her, not in front.
fact: A vocalist is a singer, especially one who sings with a band or group.
fact: Vocal means to do with the voice, so a vocalist uses their voice to make music.
fact: Phrases: lead vocalist (the main singer), backing vocalist (sings behind the main singer), guest vocalist (a singer who joins a band for a song or a show).
fact: «The guest vocalist joined the band for one song.»
fact: Vocalist is a noun, and its plural is vocalists.
exercise: «The lead vocalist sang the first verse alone.» What is a vocalist? | A person who sells tickets for a concert | *A singer, especially one who sings with a band or group | A person who plays the drums | A loud speaker on a stage
exercise: «The backing vocalists sang softly behind her.» What does backing suggest? | They were the band's drummers | They stopped singing early | They sang the main song on their own | *They supported the main singer from behind
exercise: Which phrase means a singer who joins a band for one song or show? | *Guest vocalist | Lead vocalist | Backing vocalist | Vocal teacher
test: What is the plural of vocalist? | *Vocalists | Vocalisters | Vocalist's | Vocalistes
test: What does vocal mean? | To do with the hands | To do with the feet | *To do with the voice | To do with the eyes
exam: Sam says, «Our vocalist forgot the words, so the band played on.» Who is the vocalist? | *The singer who sings with the band | The person who sells the tickets | The teacher | The drummer
